# {{ project }}

[![Workspace checks](https://github.com/{{ repository }}/actions/workflows/checks.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/{{ repository }}/actions/workflows/checks.yml)
[![Docs & Showcase](https://github.com/{{ repository }}/actions/workflows/pages.yml/badge.svg)]({{ pages_url }})

A native Android client (API 28–36, Java, zero WebView) for chatting, coding, approving actions, and customizing your workspace with your own Hermes Agent. Automatically follows your device language (**English** and **French**) with a 1-tap override and syncs your language preference to Hermes.

**[Explore the Showcase & Docs Portal →]({{ pages_url }})** · [Documentation]({{ pages_url }}docs/) · [Live Device Gallery]({{ pages_url }}walkthrough/) · [Releases](https://github.com/{{ repository }}/releases)

> **Companion server requirement:** {{ project }} requires our Hermes Agent fork at **[{{ fork_repository }}]({{ fork_url }})**. It depends on the fork’s single-host multi-profile routing (`/p/{profile}`), run-scoped instructions, Live UI modding (`ui.patch`), universal push deliveries (`mobile_deliver`), Brain Studio (memory, Smart Notes, pattern-gated habits, universal sharing, FTS5 search, skill studio, workspace files), visual approval diffs, and approved device bridge.

## What {{ project }} Does

| Pillar | Capabilities |
| --- | --- |
| **Adaptive Phone & Tablet Shell** | 4 top-level workspaces (**Discussions**, **Atelier**, **Brain / Cerveau**, **Activity / Activité**): IME-aware bottom bar on phones, **92 dp** navigation rail and dual-pane discussion sidebar (`232–360 dp`) on tablets, preserving drafts across rotation and split-screen. Includes a **Quick-Jump Command Palette** (`Ctrl+K` / `Cmd+K` or 1-tap) and **Everyday Workflows & Encrypted Templates** (strictly staging editable drafts). |
| **Concurrent Tasks & Live Health** | Run up to **8 concurrent discussions per profile** simultaneously with live per-thread status badges, individual Stop controls, and multi-task Android 16 Live Updates progress—backed by a **Live Connection Doctor** checking server reachability, companion fork capabilities, push, updates, ambient access, and language sync with a redacted safe report. |
| **Coding, Diffs & Duplex Voice** | Streaming replies with rich Markdown, paged syntax-highlighted `CodeReader`, visual hunk-level approval diffs, hands-free **Duplex Voice** plus offline/system dictation and offline speech playback. |
| **Live UI Modding & On-the-Fly Widgets** | Ask Hermes to adapt a screen, tune colors (WCAG-AA `4.5:1` Day/Night invariant), or build an interactive tool (`ui.patch` + Surfaces v2). Preview diffs, apply atomically, roll back any revision, or pin profile-scoped Home Screen Widgets. [Live UI & Widgets](docs/live-ui-and-widgets.md) |
| **Android 16 OS & Vault Security** | Live Updates notifications for active runs, Quick Settings Tile, App Shortcuts, Class-3 Biometric Vault (`BIOMETRIC_STRONG` / `DEVICE_CREDENTIAL`), persisted wrong-passphrase exponential backoff, configurable lock grace periods, and atomic profile wipe on forget. |
| **Brain Studio & Universal Sharing** | Edit Hermes’s Memory (`MEMORY.md` / `USER.md`), capture AI Smart Notes, review pattern-gated habit suggestions (`>= 3` occurrences), search all history via FTS5, manage Skills, browse Workspace Files & Git diffs, pin/fork/export threads, and share **7 resource kinds** (`note`, `skill`, `surface`, `widget`, `tool`, `artifact`, `session`) with other users on the same server. [Brain Studio & Sharing](docs/brain-and-sharing.md) |
| **Zero-Root Ambient Intelligence** | Strictly opt-in per profile (all OFF by default). Searchable per-app notification allowlist guarded by a fail-closed privacy filter that hard-blocks OTP/2FA codes, password managers, banking apps, and secret lockscreen notices. 1-tap Summarize, Save to Note, Calendar, Reviewed Quick-Reply, plus Now Playing media controls. [Ambient Intelligence](docs/ambient.md) |
| **Universal Push & Closed-App Delivery** | Zero-leak notifications via Firebase Cloud Messaging or self-hosted UnifiedPush (ntfy + Web Push encryption). Polls run, cron, and `mobile_state.db` delivery metadata only—titles and bodies stay on your gateway until you unlock the owning profile. Supports urgency tiers (`normal`, `high`, `silent`) and Quiet Hours. [Push & Reminders](docs/push.md) |
| **Universal Capture & 10 OS Actions** | Share text, photos (EXIF/GPS/ICC stripped into fresh sRGB pixels), documents, or camera captures into any thread. Review and launch 10 native Android actions: calendar, share sheet, map search, turn-by-turn navigation, alarm, timer, dialer, SMS, email, and contact editor. [Android Actions](docs/android-actions.md) |
| **Bilingual FR / EN Auto-Detect** | Follows Android’s system language automatically (`fr` / `en`, App Bundle language splits disabled, 1:1 XML parity) with an in-app picker that updates `Accept-Language`, `user_language`, and `PATCH /api/profile/defaults`. |
| **Single HTTPS Hostname Multi-Profile** | **One single HTTPS server hostname** (for example `https://hermes.example.com`) serves every user under `/p/<profile>` with isolated profile homes, workspaces, credentials, and 256-bit access keys—no per-user subdomains required. [Multi-Profile Deploy](docs/accounts.md) |

## Quickstart

### 1. Get the APK & Stay Up to Date

- **Signed releases (recommended):** Download `{{ release_apk }}`, `{{ checksum_file }}`, and `release.json` from [Latest GitHub Release](https://github.com/{{ repository }}/releases/latest), then verify checksum, APK signature, and GitHub build provenance. [Releases & In-App Auto-Update](docs/release.md) · [Verify a release](docs/delivery.md#verify-a-release)
- **Built-in verified in-app updates:** Open **Activity → App Updates** (**Activité → Mises à jour**) to check GitHub Releases directly from the phone. Downloads are fail-closed: the app verifies HTTPS GitHub release hosts, constant-time `SHA256SUMS` match, and matching APK signing certificate before handing off to Android’s native installer.
- **Development builds:** Open a passing [Workspace checks](https://github.com/{{ repository }}/actions/workflows/checks.yml) run and download the **android-debug** artifact (includes `app-debug.apk` and `SHA256SUMS`).

### 2. Connect a Profile on One HTTPS Host

1. Deploy our Hermes Agent fork ([{{ fork_repository }}]({{ fork_url }})) behind **one single HTTPS hostname** (`https://hermes.example.com`), routing each person to `/p/<profile>` with their own isolated home and access key. [Deploy multi-profile accounts](docs/accounts.md)
2. Open **Connect Hermes** (**Connecter Hermes**), enter a profile label, your shared HTTPS server address, your **Server profile** (**Profil serveur**) slug (the app composes `/p/<profile>` automatically), and your access key.
3. Protect the local device vault with a passphrase (and optionally enroll Class-3 Biometrics in **Activity → Security**).

## Build & Verify Locally

Requires **JDK 21**, **Android SDK** (`compileSdk` and `buildToolsVersion` in `gradle.properties`), and **Python 3.11+** (with `uv` or `pip`).

```sh
# 1. Fast host verification (docs check, CI scripts, server, deploy & verification suites in parallel)
{{ fast_check }}

# 2. Build, lint, and run Android JVM unit tests
./gradlew :app:lintDebug :app:testDebugUnitTest :app:assembleDebug :app:assembleRelease

# 3. Install on a connected device or emulator
adb install -r {{ debug_apk }}
```

Run `./gradlew :app:connectedDebugAndroidTest` against a connected Android emulator or handset to execute the full instrumentation suite.

